# Repo-wide ignores.
#
# These live at the root deliberately. infra/terraform-aws/ has its own .gitignore and
# stayed clean; infra/terraform-azure/ had none, and `terraform init` there put 580 MB of
# provider binaries into a commit — one of them 215 MB, past GitHub's hard 100 MB limit,
# which rejected the push. A per-directory ignore only protects the directories someone
# remembered to write one for, so the artifact patterns belong here where every current
# and future infra directory inherits them.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Terraform
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Provider binaries and module cache. Regenerated by `terraform init`, hundreds of MB,
# and platform-specific — a darwin_arm64 provider is useless to anyone on linux_amd64.
.terraform/

# State. Plaintext secrets, and it belongs in the remote backend rather than in git.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# Real variable values. Only the .example files are committed.
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars

# Plan output — can contain resolved secret values.
#
# Both patterns are needed. `*.tfplan` does not match a file named exactly `tfplan`, and
# `-out=tfplan` is the form every tutorial uses — including the snippet in
# docs/ENHANCEMENT-PLAN.md task 6. `git check-ignore tfplan` returned nothing until this line
# existed, which means the one file the comment above is about was the one file not covered.
*.tfplan
tfplan

crash.log
crash.*.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

build/
*.zip

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/

# Linter/test caches. Regenerated on every run and machine-specific.
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example run artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# e2e-agent writes the full prompt, response, and user id into every audit entry and one
# provenance file per request. Both are produced by running the demo, and both are exactly
# the kind of content that should never reach a commit. The Terraform patterns above guard
# against a 580 MB push; these guard against a smaller and more embarrassing one.
examples/e2e-agent/audit.log
examples/e2e-agent/provenance/

# rag-* build a local index on first run.
examples/rag-faiss/index.faiss
examples/rag-langchain/index.faiss

# checkpoint-agent writes its crash-recovery checkpoint here on first run, and state.tmp is
# the scratch file its atomic write renames from. Committing the checkpoint ships one machine's
# run history to everyone who clones: the file arrived in git holding eight actions left over
# from a test run, so `agent.py action1` — the example's own documented first command — replied
# "Already completed: action1" and demonstrated nothing. The file is regenerated by running the
# example, which is the whole point of it.
examples/checkpoint-agent/state.json
examples/checkpoint-agent/state.tmp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated analysis artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# graphify builds a knowledge graph of the repository into this directory. It is derived
# entirely from the tracked source, regenerates with `graphify`, and is large — a ~3.8 MB
# graph.json and a ~3.1 MB self-contained graph.html, plus an extraction cache. Committing
# it means a multi-megabyte diff on every run, of a file nobody reviews.
graphify-out/

# docs-preview is the output of .github/scripts/docs_preview.py. The docs-preview workflow
# uploads it as a CI artifact; a local run writes it into the repo root, so it is ignored
# rather than committed. Remove it with `rm -rf docs-preview` after a local build.
docs-preview/

# audit-claims.txt is raw grep output produced during repository audits. It is a scratch
# artifact, never source — the durable findings live in docs/REPOSITORY-DISCREPANCIES.md.
audit-claims.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

.DS_Store
